  "result": "I implemented `slugify` in `src/strings.js` and added 11 tests for it in `test/strings.test.js`. `npm test` passes: all 13 tests, including the 2 that were already there.\n\n**How it works, in order:**\n1. Lowercase the text.\n2. Replace `đ` with `d` directly. Unicode doesn't treat `đ` as a letter plus an accent mark, so the general accent-stripping step would miss it.\n3. Split letters from their accent marks and delete the marks.\n4. Turn each run of characters that aren't `a-z` or `0-9` into one `-`.\n5. Remove hyphens at the start and end.\n6. Cut to 50 characters, then remove any hyphens left at the end.\n\n**The tests cover:** Vietnamese text (`Tiếng Việt có dấu` → `tieng-viet-co-dau`), `Đ`/`đ`, French and Spanish accents, collapsing mixed symbols, trimming, digits, empty and symbol-only input, the 50-character limit, a cut that lands on a hyphen, and a cut that falls inside a word.\n\n**One limitation:** a few Latin letters, such as `ø`, `ß`, `æ` and `ł`, can't be split into a base letter plus an accent mark the way `ế` or `é` can. Only `đ` gets a manual replacement, so these others are dropped and treated as separators: `Straße` becomes `stra-e`. If you need them, I can add a small replacement table (for example `ß`→`ss`, `ø`→`o`).\n\nI haven't committed anything.",
